(6922222, 1039925, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I do like low fidelity images and this certainly qualifies - I hope this turns out to be a pinhole or zone plate affair.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: However... for me, the highlights over-dominate, the coloration isn''t that interesting and the subject matter itself a little ''straight up''.<br/> <br/>Overall: I like what the image stands for but I''m not keen on this presentation. Sorry.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I do like low fidelity images and this certainly qualifies - I hope this turns out to be a pinhole or zone plate affair. Critical stuff: However... for me, the highlights over-dominate, the coloration isn''t that interesting and the subject matter itself a little ''straight up''. Overall: I like what the image stands for but I''m not keen on this presentation. Sorry.', '2012-12-04 08:06:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6922226, 1043229, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I really like the use of blur in images and this is a particularly dynamic example. I like how the trails paint out the rhythm of walking. The red coloration provides a great accent against the great sky and pavement.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I think I would''ve preferred in straightened - as odd as that sounds for an image such as this, I think straight verticals would emphasise the chaos and flow of the movement.<br/> <br/>Overall: Interesting shot.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I really like the use of blur in images and this is a particularly dynamic example. I like how the trails paint out the rhythm of walking. The red coloration provides a great accent against the great sky and pavement. Critical stuff: I think I would''ve preferred in straightened - as odd as that sounds for an image such as this, I think straight verticals would emphasise the chaos and flow of the movement. Overall: Interesting shot.', '2012-12-04 08:10:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6922228, 1043075, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Wow now that is what it feels like to be ''on top of the world''! The majesty of the mountains and the being above the cloud deck looks to be both an exhilarating and humbling experience at the same time. Capturing the person in the shot adds a human experience to the landscape and gives it a sense of scale.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Wow now that is what it feels like to be ''on top of the world''! The majesty of the mountains and the being above the cloud deck looks to be both an exhilarating and humbling experience at the same time. Capturing the person in the shot adds a human experience to the landscape and gives it a sense of scale.', '2012-12-04 08:12:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6922230, 1042196, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Fascinating image - so rich in its presentation of colour. The degree of blur is fantastic - oodles of mystery but with maintenance of the shape of the figure. I feel we are high, looking over his shoulder; I''m intrigued by the red thing by his right foot (assuming I''m right about the orientation) - is it a pot plant? Ahead into the light, the sense of mystery is almost mystical - like a light in the woods - alien abduction dream incarnate!<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nope<br/> <br/>Overall: Very successful image.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Fascinating image - so rich in its presentation of colour. The degree of blur is fantastic - oodles of mystery but with maintenance of the shape of the figure. I feel we are high, looking over his shoulder; I''m intrigued by the red thing by his right foot (assuming I''m right about the orientation) - is it a pot plant? Ahead into the light, the sense of mystery is almost mystical - like a light in the woods - alien abduction dream incarnate! Critical stuff: Nope Overall: Very successful image.', '2012-12-04 08:14:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6922233, 1042628, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Great silhouette''s of these two lovers kissing under the Eiffel Tower. The whole look and mood of the composition speaks ''love in Paris''. Nicely done.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Great silhouette''s of these two lovers kissing under the Eiffel Tower. The whole look and mood of the composition speaks ''love in Paris''. Nicely done.', '2012-12-04 08:15:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6922247, 1040739, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Love the hazy clouds and overall warm golden hue of the photo. I love how the plane and the birds are together here. Nature and Man sharing the skies was one of the thoughts that struck me when I viewed this picture. The both seem to be traveling to the same destination in that they look to be going in the same direction. Wonderful capture of something that is seldom seen.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Love the hazy clouds and overall warm golden hue of the photo. I love how the plane and the birds are together here. Nature and Man sharing the skies was one of the thoughts that struck me when I viewed this picture. The both seem to be traveling to the same destination in that they look to be going in the same direction. Wonderful capture of something that is seldom seen.', '2012-12-04 08:20:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6922251, 1043384, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Great capture of the interaction of the man and the birds. Love the open hand offering food, the one bird staring up at him wondering if it should trust, and another bird captured in flight coming in for a landing. B&amp;W tones are excellent here. My one critique is that I think the photo could be even stronger if you cropped out 1/5 of the right side to get rid of the distracting Caution sign. That would keep the focus solely on your main subjects in the composition.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Great capture of the interaction of the man and the birds. Love the open hand offering food, the one bird staring up at him wondering if it should trust, and another bird captured in flight coming in for a landing. B&W tones are excellent here. My one critique is that I think the photo could be even stronger if you cropped out 1/5 of the right side to get rid of the distracting Caution sign. That would keep the focus solely on your main subjects in the composition.', '2012-12-04 08:25:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6922252, 1043326, 101668, '<td valign="top">This holds my attention for more than its beauty but also because it speaks to my heart being farmers and suffering a dry season but this seems to be ripe wheat fields which are waiting to be combined, won''t be wanting rain now!</td>', 'This holds my attention for more than its beauty but also because it speaks to my heart being farmers and suffering a dry season but this seems to be ripe wheat fields which are waiting to be combined, won''t be wanting rain now!', '2012-12-04 08:28:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6922253, 1042917, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Wow, this is such a dynamic and bold fashion model shot. Love the angle and the sassy pose. The angle and the color &amp; texture of the dress makes it appear to me that she is emerging from the rock cliff. A spirit of nature and a by her stance &amp; expression a force to be reckoned with. Excellent job on the lighting and composition of the piece.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Wow, this is such a dynamic and bold fashion model shot. Love the angle and the sassy pose. The angle and the color & texture of the dress makes it appear to me that she is emerging from the rock cliff. A spirit of nature and a by her stance & expression a force to be reckoned with. Excellent job on the lighting and composition of the piece.', '2012-12-04 08:29:28.000000', NULL, 1),
